What does HTML stand for?	Hypertext Markup Language
What is HTML mainly used for?	HTML is used to mark up and structure the sections of a web page, such as headings, paragraphs, lists, and other areas
What does CSS stand for?	Cascading Style Sheets
What is CSS mainly used for?	CSS controls the visual styling of a web page, such as fonts, colors, layout, and text direction
What is JavaScript mainly used for in web development?	JavaScript adds functionality and interactivity to web pages. It can also change HTML content and CSS styling
What are the three main technologies used in a web page?	HTML, CSS, and JavaScript
What does a browser do when a web address is typed in?	The browser makes a request to a server, and the server returns a web page
What is an HTML tag?	An HTML tag is a piece of markup used to identify parts of a web page
How can you tell the difference between an opening tag and a closing tag?	A closing tag has a forward slash as the second character, while an opening tag does not
What kind of slash is used in closing HTML tags?	A forward slash
What word in "Hypertext Markup Language" was emphasized as most important to remember?	Markup
What is an HTML element?	An element is the opening tag, its content, and the closing tag taken together
What can opening tags include besides the tag name?	Opening tags can include attributes, which provide additional information to the browser
What are self-closing tags used for?	They are used for tags that do not need content between opening and closing tags, such as an image reference
What is the purpose of the HTML head section?	The head contains information about the page that is usually not visible and is mainly for the browser
What does the HTML title tag do?	The title tag sets the page title shown in the browser tab
What does an HTTP status code of 200 mean?	It means the request was successful and the server returned the requested information
What does an HTTP status code of 301 mean?	It means Moved Permanently
Why doesn't a web page appear all at once when it loads?	Because the browser progressively processes the HTML and other resources as they arrive
What was said about the page description in HTML?	The description helps browsers and search engines understand what the page is about, and it can be used in search results
What is a favicon?	A favicon is the small icon shown on a browser tab for a website
Does CSS change the content of a page?	No. CSS changes how the content looks visually, not the content itself
What are some examples of things CSS can control?	CSS can control font size, font style, colors, positioning, layout, and text direction
Did the live CSS edits change the actual website for everyone?	No. The edits only changed the local browser view during the demonstration
What browser tool was used to run JavaScript directly on the page?	The Console in the browser developer tools
In one sentence, what is HTML for?	HTML is for marking and structuring the sections and content of a web page
In one sentence, what is CSS for?	CSS is for controlling the visual style and layout of a web page
In one sentence, what is JavaScript for?	JavaScript is a programming language that adds functionality and can manipulate both HTML and CSS
Which technology handles structure?	HTML = structure/content
Which technology handles style?	CSS = style/presentation
Which technology handles behavior?	JavaScript = behavior/functionality